(a) 1970 and 1971: One Classification Officer, (i) BA; (ii) Transferred from St. Vincent de Paul. Served in Quebec Provincial Corrections; (iii) 1970, $10,143-511,525; 1971, $10,701-312,159. 1972: Two Classification Officers, (i) and
(ii)	see 1970; (iii) $11,236-$ 12,767. (i) Grade 12; (ii) Correctional Officer, Leclerc Institution. Courses in Social Work;
(iii)	$11,236-512,767. 1973: One Classification Officer, (i) Grade 12; (ii) Correctional Officer, Leclerc Institution. Courses in Social Work; (iii) $12,416-514,108. 1974: Three Classification Officers, (i) and (ii) see 1973; (iii) $13,658-$15,519. (i) BA; (ii) Teacher, Ste. Therese College; (iii) $13,658-515,519. (i) BA; (ii) University of Laval (direct entry); (iii) $13,658-515,519. 1975: Four Classification Officers. (i) BSC; (ii) Transferred from Federal Training Centre. Professor at Laval University; (iii) $15,886-518,052. (i) Grade 13; (ii) Living Unit Officer, Correctional Officer, Leclerc Institution; (iii) $13,658-515,519. (i) BA; (ii) Graduate student, Laval University; (iii) $13,658-515,519. (i) BA; MA; (ii) Department of Health, Province of Quebec; (iii) $ 13,658-$ 15,519. (b) None.
